9367-5fe1-9cea-0be46faa4ebc" :question/math-academy-id "q-33067" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(5,0,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,4,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨5,0,-3⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨2,4,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ & =⟨5,0,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,4,-1⟩ & =13 \\\\ 2x+4y-z & =13 \\\\ 2x+4y-z-13 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-33067/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33067"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33926/selection/26ca39921f58e680858ce38fd7e417b33e62d33acfb96cd288b85719d34e35c3" :answer/id #uuid "59f14b86-3fe8-52f4-b9c8-dbbfe3669e38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+3z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33926/selection/04bcf856ae34834866add0e22ab5dfff6d44c06cbbb3d079412cf984f61e0c82" :answer/id #uuid "8101687d-7ccb-52d3-a02f-0c5359b90ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33926/selection/c13bb3bbfc00437bcfa5ff567b85ecc6694a16942fc2dc9ee16db24da43a70be" :answer/id #uuid "168ede94-970d-55eb-9df2-b1ae2213784b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-5y+z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33926/selection/7e23db853b67be10b0609ee661e2455b1bf26da8872aa9670e1edbf57009ce5c" :answer/id #uuid "cf820b1a-e763-5ae9-a87b-16e8093772f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33926/selection/433cb023ac9e97324eb19e3fbeae9ea986c28f4f23e56d0b0739e1c92e1c6c51" :answer/id #uuid "8b2fcc60-90c3-5609-bfed-6442fa453c39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2y+z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33926/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "00a3b9d1-0ad0-5d22-99a4-a2440d1b0130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33926/selection/04bcf856ae34834866add0e22ab5dfff6d44c06cbbb3d079412cf984f61e0c82" :answer-field/choices ["q-33926/selection/26ca39921f58e680858ce38fd7e417b33e62d33acfb96cd288b85719d34e35c3" "q-33926/selection/04bcf856ae34834866add0e22ab5dfff6d44c06cbbb3d079412cf984f61e0c82" "q-33926/selection/c13bb3bbfc00437bcfa5ff567b85ecc6694a16942fc2dc9ee16db24da43a70be" "q-33926/selection/7e23db853b67be10b0609ee661e2455b1bf26da8872aa9670e1edbf57009ce5c" "q-33926/selection/433cb023ac9e97324eb19e3fbeae9ea986c28f4f23e56d0b0739e1c92e1c6c51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33926" :question/id #uuid "20f01ed6-ba75-58b7-8c4e-708e14bec166" :question/math-academy-id "q-33926" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,0,3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,0,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨1,0,3⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,1⟩ & =⟨1,0,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0,1⟩ & =5 \\\\ 2x+z & =5 \\\\ 2x+z-5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-33926/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33926"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70805/selection/2a2f6fbe98f3c916421e1a67da589ccb1cbff5e461345d00fd1ff6a047577594" :answer/id #uuid "97db5536-94e6-57c9-932b-b7d1dd8ab302" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y+2z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70805/selection/4473a231f0a0f05d89b059e038522a6beeb4fee79e812c144e29e700050cd808" :answer/id #uuid "44dca2f2-e0dc-50b3-8855-d2bc9b7b3045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+3z+8=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70805/selection/bc1f3a9b046874f19b4ce7531ec9ac7daea03418198d50698f86b5d89b60e1a7" :answer/id #uuid "862e7072-e0fd-5084-b3f3-06155608d474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+3z+5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70805/selection/45079bf32d3b47ef665e62bbd273b10699ebb90e49960a4330db1f9babeedd56" :answer/id #uuid "d9153e5f-3cdd-5dc5-8a10-ed35868113d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+3z+6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70805/selection/9dce2aecab2a13b060645cbc64a302cba7c65b8ad5f793103e3ad003bf7d1d4a" :answer/id #uuid "eaf6de68-de37-58f0-a72d-0d0b902321de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x+y-2z+6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70805/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd31e76-57ed-504c-b930-3502ff9a51eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70805/selection/45079bf32d3b47ef665e62bbd273b10699ebb90e49960a4330db1f9babeedd56" :answer-field/choices ["q-70805/selection/2a2f6fbe98f3c916421e1a67da589ccb1cbff5e461345d00fd1ff6a047577594" "q-70805/selection/4473a231f0a0f05d89b059e038522a6beeb4fee79e812c144e29e700050cd808" "q-70805/selection/bc1f3a9b046874f19b4ce7531ec9ac7daea03418198d50698f86b5d89b60e1a7" "q-70805/selection/45079bf32d3b47ef665e62bbd273b10699ebb90e49960a4330db1f9babeedd56" "q-70805/selection/9dce2aecab2a13b060645cbc64a302cba7c65b8ad5f793103e3ad003bf7d1d4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70805" :question/id #uuid "c9388b78-08c8-50f9-9be6-ffeb2395d72f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70805" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-1,1,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=i+j+3k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-1,1,-2⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨1,1,3⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ & =⟨-1,1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ & =-6 \\\\ x+y+3z & =-6 \\\\ x+y+3z+6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70805/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70805"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33162/selection/00c0b2b63119000fb0222f33a0023dd13e6404dd6e41fc1b3738936203888a3b" :answer/id #uuid "19fc3d16-e8e1-5339-bebe-dbfb05c66204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-5y+z+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33162/selection/e36d5fa391cf2431f472c55a588abd3d48fff56878e2f97a3becec7ffcbeda49" :answer/id #uuid "11d2e9ed-28d4-5d80-a01d-2565bfaf0a6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3x+4z+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33162/selection/38cf3227dbe01a9d4f40f1e2a57a7f30e100362e26bf35662d9f457b68833397" :answer/id #uuid "90c65b6b-1e8c-5704-b492-3ae24d0a7c53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3x+y+4z-1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33162/selection/a91a3b4386cebb53c8cf35e702a26041532322ed39375ad1d0d41d51ab0f03b2" :answer/id #uuid "199582ba-c325-595d-b2f4-33c4e5cdfdcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-5y+2z+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33162/selection/ca0208bb55f48e101b3d923ebcfd702cc771b8fd369ffef3aa576112de50a857" :answer/id #uuid "ec30125d-b6ec-57f0-a7ed-21cb20936f89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5x+3y+2z+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33162/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "81bbdfc3-17f8-59b1-be4b-9724719cc071" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33162/selection/a91a3b4386cebb53c8cf35e702a26041532322ed39375ad1d0d41d51ab0f03b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-33162/selection/00c0b2b63119000fb0222f33a0023dd13e6404dd6e41fc1b3738936203888a3b" "q-33162/selection/e36d5fa391cf2431f472c55a588abd3d48fff56878e2f97a3becec7ffcbeda49" "q-33162/selection/38cf3227dbe01a9d4f40f1e2a57a7f30e100362e26bf35662d9f457b68833397" "q-33162/selection/a91a3b4386cebb53c8cf35e702a26041532322ed39375ad1d0d41d51ab0f03b2" "q-33162/selection/ca0208bb55f48e101b3d923ebcfd702cc771b8fd369ffef3aa576112de50a857"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33162" :question/id #uuid "c43b9462-37b6-5478-904d-7307590edba1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33162" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,0,4)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-3,0,4⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-5,2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-5,2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =⟨-3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-1 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z & =-1 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-33162/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33162"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33165"] :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(8,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x+2}{4}=\\frac{y-1}{3}=\\frac{z-2}{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨8,3,-1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨4,3,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨4,3,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =⟨8,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =42 \\\\ 4x+3y-z & =42 \\\\ 4x+3y-z-42 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-336213/selection/417e9a129f89861f245513b2fbb92a21f1e5cdf5a93c079fafe36542cb88ce81" :answer/id #uuid "15b52294-a5b4-582b-aa07-7a85d3e4b93b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4y+2z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336213/selection/f331f0a6e57c418071945ac4c04f6aa29421aabbd7129670c9382f9b3c5e698c" :answer/id #uuid "7281ddb0-fe67-5741-a26f-7de06840a772" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4y-z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336213/selection/14bc1bbc1b0a28bd35743841e160dedb70ff7c74b7d0ba1ff33c794372a50c58" :answer/id #uuid "05b2db7f-2ae1-5b39-b4d8-554a15eee51d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4y+z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336213/selection/14f7e564d5f9ec8cbe8d5e196982b88d92325f00be8caeb04414a744e91b51f7" :answer/id #uuid "a253867a-ddb0-56d8-9ad9-21f2a16c1aa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4y+z-3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336213/selection/f5fc0661b849922248bc9ee2b47ec9280d015507e34d6165c6dd8bc1440baca3" :answer/id #uuid "50d6ccf2-85d5-50dc-aab3-938de324058c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4y+z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336213/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bec8bf2-432e-55fc-bd19-7d187da4a49a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-336213/selection/14bc1bbc1b0a28bd35743841e160dedb70ff7c74b7d0ba1ff33c794372a50c58" :answer-field/choices ["q-336213/selection/417e9a129f89861f245513b2fbb92a21f1e5cdf5a93c079fafe36542cb88ce81" "q-336213/selection/f331f0a6e57c418071945ac4c04f6aa29421aabbd7129670c9382f9b3c5e698c" "q-336213/selection/14bc1bbc1b0a28bd35743841e160dedb70ff7c74b7d0ba1ff33c794372a50c58" "q-336213/selection/14f7e564d5f9ec8cbe8d5e196982b88d92325f00be8caeb04414a744e91b51f7" "q-336213/selection/f5fc0661b849922248bc9ee2b47ec9280d015507e34d6165c6dd8bc1440baca3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336213" :question/id #uuid "5476e4b7-9d7c-5e18-af79-26ad89717789" :question/math-academy-id "q-336213" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,1,0)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ y=-2+4t \\\\ z=3+t\\end{aligned}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,1,0⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨0,4,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨0,4,1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ & =4 \\\\ 4y+z & =4 \\\\ 4y+z-4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336213/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336213"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336111/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "75f97724-6015-5d4f-87ac-0be426a764c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336111/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "822ca1cd-0722-519d-9885-9d8ed65c1c2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336111/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-336111/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336111/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e5806d8d-242f-5177-aaed-7461250dc45b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336111/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ba7856-4e39-520b-8fd7-e93a3a291acb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336111/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-336111/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336111/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "43d948d7-d5d5-5723-b0e6-cf140ffb4b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336111/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "737b3577-6bf4-51a3-8235-bb1a49a894db" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336111/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-336111/field-3/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336111" :question/id #uuid "180db9bd-178c-5bc0-8e09-b035c76a3c3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-336111" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,4,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=-1+2t \\\\ y=5+3t \\\\ z=7-t\\end{aligned}.$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,x\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$y\\,-\\,z\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-3,4,1⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨2,3,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨2,3,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,-1⟩ & =⟨-3,4,1⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,-1⟩ & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,-1⟩ & =5 \\\\ 2x+3y-z & =5 \\\\ 2x+3y-z-5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336111/field-1" "q-336111/field-2" "q-336111/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336111"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128376/selection/4e471fc9e7e6b62e0484a9e60798d59771b4d2b7234a828587f58db4cb430b40" :answer/id #uuid "e2594059-827b-55b5-8208-d8a00afb06f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y+z-6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128376/selection/674681c16cac1e901f0c67b1f31cad7430b54c7033dec070a2426e42fabcc30f" :answer/id #uuid "45896f8a-7944-531c-893e-522a8af1d878" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y-z+3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128376/selection/f0e4842b47eefaf98666ce29b99c529d9900df2551472aba1786045bccd7d013" :answer/id #uuid "f8f4ca43-67ad-54b5-88d2-654580ef9be5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+z-3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128376/selection/d8f7e56bab31a37b0420d2e637a617a09c8a1a234f0dd0a1aa5f88c68bad7fc9" :answer/id #uuid "0f03d236-ebd3-5571-9e7b-706d5d055a76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y-z+6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128376/selection/626dbd2d70e528c488b006aa2f2860ca4bcca91937ef202d28a4621e1021b56c" :answer/id #uuid "773ac187-9f1a-5da9-b359-cb81e454cded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x-y+z+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128376/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3cf2ec3-b08f-5c28-b812-c14f968dc777" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128376/selection/d8f7e56bab31a37b0420d2e637a617a09c8a1a234f0dd0a1aa5f88c68bad7fc9" :answer-field/choices ["q-128376/selection/4e471fc9e7e6b62e0484a9e60798d59771b4d2b7234a828587f58db4cb430b40" "q-128376/selection/674681c16cac1e901f0c67b1f31cad7430b54c7033dec070a2426e42fabcc30f" "q-128376/selection/f0e4842b47eefaf98666ce29b99c529d9900df2551472aba1786045bccd7d013" "q-128376/selection/d8f7e56bab31a37b0420d2e637a617a09c8a1a234f0dd0a1aa5f88c68bad7fc9" "q-128376/selection/626dbd2d70e528c488b006aa2f2860ca4bcca91937ef202d28a4621e1021b56c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128376" :question/id #uuid "73a51566-e903-5429-a833-3a965966f7dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-128376" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-5,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=3+t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=7-t\\end{aligned}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-5,2⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨1,1,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨1,1,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =-6 \\\\ x+y-z & =-6 \\\\ x+y-z+6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128376/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128376"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336225/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "53e214a7-efc7-522f-9b20-60311710ef8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336225/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3347e566-35a5-50a3-837d-05ebc285bf1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336225/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-336225/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336225/field-2/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "5288c902-d56c-5ce1-8bee-d4b43b5daaa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336225/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "657fcdb9-feaa-5ed7-aa02-89fdfff374f3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336225/field-2/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer-field/choices ["q-336225/field-2/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336225/field-3/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "91965d3f-b50a-57df-9e23-28c61ef3ee7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336225/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "de0fe834-bf1d-556d-9fd9-5ed7a2506cab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336225/field-3/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-336225/field-3/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336225" :question/id #uuid "e29c766d-a204-551a-be78-6b62beba7d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-336225" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $5x-7y+4z+20=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,$\n{{field-2}}\n,\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨5,-7,4⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-7y+4z+20 & =0 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{5}{4}x+\\frac{7}{4}y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-5.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-5)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-5⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-5⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,-7,4⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336225/field-1" "q-336225/field-2" "q-336225/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128400/selection/6ffd9696c6dd55497b30f1907d31ef114532545b14f0425f6bd23289d3176176" :answer/id #uuid "990652fd-70a4-5d37-8d07-9f27ede2f633" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,1,0⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128400/selection/04f30da3df3beb4b3c7e89bf08979488ae3bd88e16352498d747774da3bc703a" :answer/id #uuid "9b591e97-568e-54e1-b2ff-3b25d6f8a868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,-3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,0⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128400/selection/4486f4ed51654e8fb5b5d83d5f29996682c28d827901165d43d25b5fcb0c5b31" :answer/id #uuid "1f0a58eb-4f3d-598b-8f9e-aaeb7207b6f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,6,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128400/selection/d8aef546f278f2c64eb873a4f91ced94a584675b208874ba8056a51f394f7d02" :answer/id #uuid "75ce8e92-2131-5643-828a-adff4a01a923" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,-6,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,0,1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128400/selection/3383d96715e95489eaa68e33fc1cc375f27dc5c8c680b1daf4d5e92ba912a36e" :answer/id #uuid "8bfbc34b-25a5-5d23-bc9c-f80e7085e552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,9,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨-7,0,1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128400/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "10b864a4-1db5-53bd-a23e-5baed302ea88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128400/selection/6ffd9696c6dd55497b30f1907d31ef114532545b14f0425f6bd23289d3176176" :answer-field/choices ["q-128400/selection/6ffd9696c6dd55497b30f1907d31ef114532545b14f0425f6bd23289d3176176" "q-128400/selection/04f30da3df3beb4b3c7e89bf08979488ae3bd88e16352498d747774da3bc703a" "q-128400/selection/4486f4ed51654e8fb5b5d83d5f29996682c28d827901165d43d25b5fcb0c5b31" "q-128400/selection/d8aef546f278f2c64eb873a4f91ced94a584675b208874ba8056a51f394f7d02" "q-128400/selection/3383d96715e95489eaa68e33fc1cc375f27dc5c8c680b1daf4d5e92ba912a36e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128400" :question/id #uuid "a275fd86-a21a-5ef1-ae5c-9df806e069b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128400" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $7x+y-3=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨7,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+y-3 & =0 \\\\ y & =3-7x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$, we get $y=3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,3,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,3,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,1,0⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128400/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128400"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336239/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "df17996d-5bda-5fb6-948d-2259f9ade96a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336239/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ecca9ad-3016-56d2-93c3-072fb1ce2ff1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336239/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-336239/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336239/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "22dd3d82-bfef-548e-b8e1-1470fac71c64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336239/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "17945930-eb69-5477-91ee-84c5615f76a4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336239/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-336239/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336239/field-3/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "0b6bf230-3342-5f4c-a57a-e0a78d873669" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336239/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "302ab8b7-2c4e-5a79-92a5-5ccbacd014ef" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336239/field-3/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-336239/field-3/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336239" :question/id #uuid "34fb864d-1d68-5d55-91b9-7781b21f48c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-336239" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $9x-3y+6=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,,0$\n\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨$\n{{field-2}}\n,\n{{field-3}}\n$,0⟩=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨9,-3,0⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3y+6 & =0 \\\\ -3y & =-9x-6 \\\\ y & =3x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$, we get $y=2.$ Hence, the point $P(0,2,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,2,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨9,-3,0⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-336239/field-1" "q-336239/field-2" "q-336239/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336239"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "5e800bf1-d28a-5a53-a920-d469452ec071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e4df9772-3f1b-50ef-82a6-bd28b0cf7e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "66b2c1da-3311-5fce-8876-7111c97ae2b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336220/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-336220/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-336220/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d163a137-3ef1-5244-b287-5634e8b6882d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "33ebb38b-e5f7-56c8-9df7-d453025c72f1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336220/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-336220/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "22c3b04b-3341-55b5-905b-1537aa5d1989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8c9445d-da75-541b-a9ab-a99ea221973f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336220/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-336220/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336220" :question/id #uuid "8a835807-097c-577a-9751-b96b199e051b" :question/math-academy-id "q-336220" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $3x+y+2z+4=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨$ \n{{field-2}}\n$,1\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨3,1,2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y+2z+4 & =0 \\\\ 2z & =-3x-y-4 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-2.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-2)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨3,1,2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336220/field-1" "q-336220/field-2" "q-336220/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312/field-1/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "ed723e51-f1a8-57b1-8bcc-cbd523f467cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "778b5a41-2ec5-55c3-b9ae-e8c86cf0ff20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "904b214a-ae22-5da8-80b3-34896b7bc41c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326312/field-1/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer-field/choices ["q-326312/field-1/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" "q-326312/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "1393e66b-02fc-5824-8c21-c9d22567df56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c61baff-428f-5056-b452-d1bac27bc5ce" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326312/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-326312/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312/field-3/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d" :answer/id #uuid "6e575f31-f881-5e2d-8d93-b41a75073669" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "35957583-1ed3-5158-8d03-b280590e6b8c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326312/field-3/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d" :answer-field/choices ["q-326312/field-3/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326312" :question/id #uuid "11d73e76-733c-5c1a-b58a-cd0a522da6dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-326312" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨1,-2,-5⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,1,-7⟩.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$y+z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-3,2,4⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =19i+7j+k \\\\  & =⟨19,7,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ & =⟨-3,2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ & =-39\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨19,7,1⟩ & =-39 \\\\ 19x+7y+z & =-39 \\\\ 19x+7y+z+39 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-326312/field-1" "q-326312/field-2" "q-326312/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0efe5b11-2