sure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336450" :question/id #uuid "736653a1-5df9-5c46-8da4-cc6725fd4151" :question/math-academy-id "q-336450" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-4,3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨1,-3,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,4,-1⟩.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+\\,y\\,+$\n{{field-2}} \n$z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨2,-4,3⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =11i+1j+4k \\\\  & =⟨11,1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨11,1,4⟩ & =⟨2,-4,3⟩\\cdot ⟨11,1,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨11,1,4⟩ & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨11,1,4⟩ & =30 \\\\ 11x+y+4z & =30 \\\\ 11x+y+4z-30 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336450/field-1" "q-336450/field-2" "q-336450/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0efe5b11-2c87-58e9-bf7c-e1eecb07adf2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336450"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70833/selection/31be378364e6562e9c5a8c3e6600f7d72914d49ae1af881d0cfb5d240e0e4207" :answer/id #uuid "790d0521-874e-51d0-b6c6-419d062acbdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+3y-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70833/selection/d